## 2. Database Schema & Tables

### A. `registrations` Table

Stores incoming orders submitted by business owners through the website's onboarding form. This acts as an initial intake queue before cards are physically fulfilled.

| Column Name | Data Type | Constraints | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `id` | uuid | PRIMARY KEY | Unique identifier for the registration entry. |
| `business_name` | text | NOT NULL | Name of the business (e.g., "Cafe Bloom"). |
| `city_location` | text | NOT NULL | City and state of the business. |
| `whatsapp_number` | text | NOT NULL | Contact number for order follow-ups. |
| `card_quantity` | text | NULL | Selected pack size (e.g., 1, 3, 5, 10). |
| `destination_url` | text | NOT NULL | The target redirect link (Google Review, Instagram profile, or WhatsApp chat). |
| `platform` | text | NOT NULL | Categorization string (`google`, `instagram`, or `whatsapp`). |
| `generated_slug` | text | NOT NULL | The unique URL handle (e.g., `cafe-bloom-pune`). |
| `created_at` | timestamptz | DEFAULT `now()` | Timestamp of form submission. |

*Constraint:* `UNIQUE(generated_slug, platform)` to prevent duplicate business handles on the same platform.

### B. `clients` Table

The production roster containing active, approved links that visitors land on when tapping smart cards.

| Column Name | Data Type | Constraints | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `slug` | text | PART OF PRIMARY KEY | The routing handle. |
| `platform` | text | PART OF PRIMARY KEY | The platform identifier (`google`, `instagram`, `whatsapp`). |
| `destination_url` | text | NOT NULL | Where the user gets redirected. |
| `total_taps` | integer | DEFAULT `0` | Aggregate lifetime tap count. |
| `monthly_taps` | jsonb | DEFAULT `'{}'` | Granular tap breakdown stored by month (`{"2026-09": 14}`). |
| `yearly_taps` | jsonb | DEFAULT `'{}'` | Granular tap breakdown stored by year (`{"2026": 120}`). |
| `created_at` | timestamptz | DEFAULT `now()` | Activation timestamp. |

*Primary Key:* Composite key `(slug, platform)` allowing the same short slug to exist independently across Google, Instagram, and WhatsApp domains.

