## 3. Database Functions & Automations

### A. Automatic Client Provisioning (Trigger)

To eliminate manual entry, a database trigger automatically promotes new rows from the `registrations` intake queue into the active `clients` table the moment a form is submitted.

```sql
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.auto_approve_client()
RETURNS TRIGGER AS $$
BEGIN
  INSERT INTO public.clients (slug, platform, destination_url, total_taps, monthly_taps, yearly_taps)
  VALUES (NEW.generated_slug, NEW.platform, NEW.destination_url, 0, '{}'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb)
  ON CONFLICT (slug, platform) DO NOTHING;
  
  RETURN NEW;
END;
$$ LANGUAGE plpgsql SECURITY DEFINER;

CREATE TRIGGER on_registration_created
AFTER INSERT ON public.registrations
FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION public.auto_approve_client();

```

### B. Atomic Tap Increment RPC (`increment_tap`)

Handles race conditions when multiple users tap cards simultaneously. It safely updates aggregate totals alongside JSON-backed monthly and yearly historical buckets.

```sql
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION increment_tap(client_slug text, client_platform text)
RETURNS void AS $$
DECLARE
  current_month text := to_char(now(), 'YYYY-MM');
  current_year text := to_char(now(), 'YYYY');
  m_count int;
  y_count int;
  m_taps jsonb;
  y_taps jsonb;
BEGIN
  SELECT monthly_taps, yearly_taps,
         COALESCE((monthly_taps->>current_month)::int, 0),
         COALESCE((yearly_taps->>current_year)::int, 0)
  INTO m_taps, y_taps, m_count, y_count
  FROM public.clients
  WHERE slug = client_slug AND platform = client_platform;

  m_taps := COALESCE(m_taps, '{}'::jsonb);
  y_taps := COALESCE(y_taps, '{}'::jsonb);

  UPDATE public.clients
  SET 
    total_taps = total_taps + 1,
    monthly_taps = jsonb_set(m_taps, ARRAY[current_month], to_jsonb(m_count + 1), true),
    yearly_taps = jsonb_set(y_taps, ARRAY[current_year], to_jsonb(y_count + 1), true)
  WHERE slug = client_slug AND platform = client_platform;
END;
$$ LANGUAGE plpgsql SECURITY DEFINER;

```

### C. Live Platform Statistics RPC (`get_platform_stats`)

Aggregates active business counts and total engagement metrics dynamically based on the requesting domain's platform context.

```sql
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION get_platform_stats(req_platform text)
RETURNS jsonb AS $$
DECLARE
  biz_count integer;
  tap_count integer;
BEGIN
  SELECT count(*), COALESCE(sum(total_taps), 0)
  INTO biz_count, tap_count
  FROM public.clients
  WHERE platform = req_platform;

  RETURN jsonb_build_object(
    'businesses_onboarded', biz_count,
    'total_taps', tap_count
  );
END;
$$ LANGUAGE plpgsql SECURITY DEFINER;

```

