## 4. Security & Row Level Security (RLS)

The public project `anon` key is exposed safely on the client-side. Security is enforced entirely at the database layer via strict RLS policies and function execution grants:

```sql
-- Enable security controls
ALTER TABLE public.registrations ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE public.clients ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

-- Allow public website visitors to register orders
CREATE POLICY "Allow public inserts" ON public.registrations FOR INSERT TO anon WITHCHECK (true);

-- Allow redirection handler to query active destination links
CREATE POLICY "Allow public read" ON public.clients FOR SELECT TO anon USING (true);

-- Grant public execution rights to RPC endpoints
GRANT EXECUTE ON FUNCTION increment_tap(text, text) TO anon, public;
GRANT EXECUTE ON FUNCTION get_platform_stats(text) TO anon, public;

```

