## 5. Frontend Implementation (`js/app.js` & `404.html`)

### A. Slug Generation & Order Submission (`js/app.js`)

When a business submits the form, strings are cleaned into URL-friendly slugs, persisted to Supabase, and formatted into an order confirmation WhatsApp string:

```javascript
var baseText = city ? `${biz}-${city}` : biz;
var slug = baseText
  .toLowerCase()
  .replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-')
  .replace(/^-+|-+$/g, '');

```

### B. Redirection & Counter Execution (`404.html`)

The GitHub Pages catch-all handler parses the pathname, fetches the target destination, awaits the tap increment transaction, and completes the redirect:

```javascript
async function handleRedirect() {
  const slug = window.location.pathname.replace(/^\/+|\/+$/g, '');
  if (!slug) { window.location.replace('/'); return; }

  const { data, error } = await supabaseClient
    .from('clients')
    .select('destination_url')
    .eq('slug', slug)
    .eq('platform', 'google') // Adjusted per domain ('instagram' / 'whatsapp')
    .single();

  if (error || !data?.destination_url) {
    document.querySelector('.box').innerHTML = '<h2>Business link not found.</h2>';
    return;
  }

  await supabaseClient.rpc('increment_tap', {
    client_slug: slug,
    client_platform: 'google'
  });

  window.location.replace(data.destination_url);
}

```